{"path":"error/exception/operator=","title":"std::exception::operator=","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::exception::</span>operator=","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/error/exception/operator=","section":"error","kind":"page","summary":"Copy assignment operator. Assigns the contents of other.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n</tbody>\n<tbody class=\"t-dcl-rev\">\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-until-cxx11\">\n<td><div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">exception<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> operator<span class=\"sy1\">=</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> exception<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> other <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">throw</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> </td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx11\">(until C++11)</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">exception<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> operator<span class=\"sy1\">=</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> exception<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> other <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(constexpr since C++26)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Copy assignment operator. Assigns the contents of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code>.\n</p><p>If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> both have dynamic type <code>std::exception</code> then <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/byte/strcmp\"><span class=\"kw1154\">std::<span class=\"me2\">strcmp</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>what<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, other.<span class=\"me1\">what</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span></span></code> after assignment.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> other\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> another exception to assign the contents of\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue471\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 471</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++98\n</td>\n<td>the effects of calling <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/exception/what\">what()</a></span> after<br>assignment are implementation-defined\n</td>\n<td>required to be the same as the original<br><span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/exception/what\">what()</a></span> if the dynamic types are the same\n</td></tr></table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"error","title":"Diagnostics library"},{"path":"error/exception","title":"std::exception"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::exception::operator=","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: until C++11, since C++11. Copy assignment operator. Assigns the contents of other."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"other"},{"label":"Defect reports","note":"The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards."}]},"standards":["C++11","C++26"],"wordCount":104,"codeBlockCount":0}
